# The Unix account has to exist before its identifier can be read, and the
# whole point of reading it is that it is never written down. A name that is
# not an account is therefore a mistake worth stopping for, and nothing is
# created: the account is resolved before the entry is added, so this does not
# leave behind an entry with neither a password nor a way to bind.
ldap_create_user --system --cn "my_mail_service"            \
                 --socket-account "no_such_account"

# Expected exit status: 1
# Expected error output:

There is no "no_such_account" account on this machine.
Install the service before creating the entry it binds as, so that its
user identifier can be read rather than guessed.

# Expected LDIF:
